{"currentConversationId":"33cec2a1-b4ea-496a-9fc5-026ec9d030fa","conversations":{"e76ac38d-a63a-4d02-9ffd-c3484ed64277":{"id":"e76ac38d-a63a-4d02-9ffd-c3484ed64277","createdAtIso":"2025-07-24T20:54:21.025Z","lastInteractedAtIso":"2025-07-24T21:15:36.854Z","chatHistory":[{"status":"success","request_id":"c316899e-26b7-4106-beae-571c11edff32","request_message":"Can you please change the codebase in a way it accepts the possibility to choose the owner and the branch to download it from there instead? I may want to download from https://github.com/Lypt1x/neutralinojs or linked with another branch.","rich_text_json_repr":{"type":"doc","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Can you please change the codebase in a way it accepts the possibility to choose the owner and the branch to download it from there instead? I may want to download from https://github.com/Lypt1x/neutralinojs or linked with another branch."}]}]},"mentioned_items":[],"structured_output_nodes":[{"id":1,"type":0,"content":"I can help you modify the codebase to support custom owners and branches for downloading. Looking at the current code, I can see that the `releasesApiUrl` in `constants.js` is hardcoded to use "neutralinojs" as the owner.

Here are the changes needed:

<augment_code_snippet path="src/constants.js" mode="EDIT">
```javascript
module.exports = {
 remote: {
 binariesUrl:"https://github.com/{owner}/{repo}/releases/download/{tag}/{repo}-{tag}.zip",
 clientUrlPrefix: "https://github.com/{owner}/{repo}/releases/download/{tag}/neutralino.",
 templateUrl: "https://github.com/{template}/archive/{branch}.zip",
 releasesApiUrl: "https://api.github.com/repos/{owner}/{repo}/releases/latest",
 templateCheckUrl: "https://github.com/{template}/tree/{branch}"
 },
 // ... rest remains the same
};
```
</augment_code_snippet>

<augment_code_snippet path="src/modules/downloader.js" mode="EDIT">
```javascript
let getBinaryDownloadUrl = async (latest, owner = 'neutralinojs', repo = 'neutralinojs') => {
 const configObj = config.get();
 let version = configObj.cli.binaryVersion;

 if (!version || latest) {
 version = await getLatestVersion(owner, repo);
 config.update('cli.binaryVersion', version);
 }
 return constants.remote.binariesUrl
 .replace(/\{owner\}/g, owner)
 .replace(/\{repo\}/g, repo)
 .replace(/\{tag\}/g, utils.getVersionTag(version));
}

let getClientDownloadUrl = async (latest, types = false, owner = 'neutralinojs', repo = 'neutralino.js') => {
 const configObj = config.get();
 let version = configObj.cli.clientVersion;

 if (!version || latest) {
 if (cachedLatestClientVersion) {
 version = cachedLatestClientVersion;
 }
 else {
 version = await getLatestVersion(owner, repo);
 }
 cachedLatestClientVersion = version;
 config.update('cli.clientVersion', version);
 }

 let scriptUrl = constants.remote.clientUrlPrefix + (types ? 'd.ts' : getScriptExtension());
 return scriptUrl
 .replace(/\{owner\}/g, owner)
 .replace(/\{repo\}/g, repo)
 .replace(/\{tag\}/g, utils.getVersionTag(version));
}

module.exports.downloadTemplate = (template, branch = 'main') => {
 return new Promise((resolve, reject) => {
 let templateUrl = constants.remote.templateUrl
 .replace('{template}', template)
 .replace('{branch}', branch);
 // ... rest of function remains the same
 });
}

module.exports.downloadAndUpdateBinaries = async (latest = false, owner = 'neutralinojs', repo = 'neutralinojs') => {
 await downloadBinariesFromRelease(latest, owner, repo);
 // ... rest remains the same
}

module.exports.downloadAndUpdateClient = async (latest = false, owner = 'neutralinojs', repo = 'neutralino.js') => {
 // ... existing logic with new parameters
}
```
</augment_code_snippet>

You'll also need to update the command-line interfaces to accept these new parameters. Would you like me to show you how to modify the `create`, `update`, and other commands to accept `--owner`, `--repo`, and `--branch` options?
